Why low-level? You do not use up power for spells that you cannot cast
anymore. Confusion is free. So you can also cast a high-level spell that
you forgot. The failure test is not applied, as far as I know. (It would
of course be an argument against high-level spells, if you'd get the
message "You fail to cast the spell correctly", instead of getting
confused, but I think the test whether you can remember the spell at
all, must be done before. If you fail to cast correctly, you lose power,
if you cannot cast anymore, you don't.)


